<h1>Search</h1>
<p>Searches every page on this site. The index is built at deploy time and
  queried entirely in your browser &mdash; no query is sent to a server.</p>

<noscript>
  <p class="note">Search runs in the browser, so it needs JavaScript. With it
    off, <a href="/all/">the full page listing</a> is browsable instead and
    covers exactly the same content.</p>
</noscript>

<form class="search-form" role="search" action="/search/" method="get">
  <label for="q">Search this site</label>
  <input type="search" id="q" name="q" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false"
         placeholder="canvas, PostgreSQL, earthquakes…">
  <button type="submit">Search</button>
</form>

<h2 id="results-heading">Results</h2>
<p class="search-status" id="search-status" role="status">Type a query to search.</p>
<ul class="search-results" id="search-results" aria-labelledby="results-heading"></ul>
